iommu/vt-d: force an identity domain for the IPU3 ImgU (8086:1919)

The staging ipu3-imgu driver bypasses the DMA API: it backs all buffers with
alloc_pages()/vb2_dma_sg and programs the ImgU's own internal MMU with raw
physical addresses (ipu3-mmu.c: page_to_phys(sg_page(s)); ipu3-dmamap.c:
imgu_mmu_map(mmu, iovaddr, page_to_phys(pages[i]))). The ImgU therefore emits
physical addresses on the bus and only works when its PCI device is in an
IOMMU identity/passthrough domain.

On kernels whose default domain is translated (IOMMU_DOMAIN_DMA / DMA-FQ, now
the default on VT-d) the ImgU's first streaming DMA targets an unmapped IOVA and
hard-locks the machine (no panic, physical reset required). Observed on the
Google Pixel Slate ("nocturne"): booting iommu=pt cures it completely and both
cameras stream through the hardware ISP.

Rather than require the global iommu=pt cmdline (which drops translation for
every device), scope the passthrough to the ImgU alone via device_def_domain_type
-- mirroring the existing IDENTMAP_AZALIA per-device identity handling. Every
other device (the ipu3-cio2 receiver included) keeps its translated domain.

The proper long-term fix is to port ipu3-imgu to the DMA API so it stops
emitting physical addresses; until then this quirk makes the hardware ISP usable
without a cmdline token.

Signed-off-by: BobZKernel <bobgenaw420@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c
index 849d06dfe..fda519a51 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c
@@ -1401,6 +1401,21 @@ static int device_def_domain_type(struct device *dev)
 
 		if ((iommu_identity_mapping & IDENTMAP_AZALIA) && IS_AZALIA(pdev))
 			return IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDENTITY;
+
+		/*
+		 * The Intel IPU3 ImgU (staging ipu3-imgu driver) programs its
+		 * own internal MMU with raw physical addresses and never uses
+		 * the DMA API, so it only functions in an identity/passthrough
+		 * domain. On kernels that default to a translated domain
+		 * (IOMMU_DOMAIN_DMA/-FQ) its first DMA hits an unmapped IOVA and
+		 * hard-locks the bus. Force an identity domain for just this
+		 * device -- observed on the Google Pixel Slate ("nocturne"),
+		 * where iommu=pt cures the lock; this scopes the passthrough to
+		 * the ImgU alone and leaves every other device translated.
+		 */
+		if (pdev->vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL &&
+		    pdev->device == 0x1919)
+			return IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDENTITY;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
